WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.750 line:10%
CHRISTOPHER TOWNSEND: So we
literally had stunts go and rig

00:00:03.750 --> 00:00:07.650 line:10%
up on our set with wires and
actually had these characters

00:00:07.650 --> 00:00:09.786 line:10%
being slammed around and moved.

00:00:09.786 --> 00:00:13.250 line:90%
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:13.250 --> 00:00:14.050 line:90%
 Beware my purr.

00:00:14.050 --> 00:00:14.990 line:90%
My tentacles bite.

00:00:14.990 --> 00:00:15.790 line:90%
I'm Lorraine.

00:00:15.790 --> 00:00:17.080 line:10%
 I might have
fallen from space.

00:00:17.080 --> 00:00:17.880 line:10%
I'm Langston.

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:19.295 line:10%
 Ooh, and this is
Earth's Mightiest Show.

00:00:19.295 --> 00:00:21.190 line:10%
 Where we talk about all
of the most '90s stuff

00:00:21.190 --> 00:00:22.090 line:10%
in the Marvel universe.

00:00:22.090 --> 00:00:24.520 line:84%
 Oh, and if we're going to talk
'90s, let's talk about this.

00:00:24.520 --> 00:00:26.410 line:90%
Higher, further, faster, baby.

00:00:26.410 --> 00:00:30.070 line:84%
Marvel Studios' Captain Marvel
is now available on digital HD.

00:00:30.070 --> 00:00:33.700 line:84%
And it's coming to Blu-ray
and DVD on June 11.

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:34.913 line:84%
I'm obsessed.
- Oh, listen.

00:00:34.913 --> 00:00:36.580 line:84%
I can't wait for all the
extras, the blooper reel,

00:00:36.580 --> 00:00:37.960 line:90%
deleted scenes, all the stuff.

00:00:37.960 --> 00:00:38.950 line:90%
I want more, please.

00:00:38.950 --> 00:00:39.910 line:90%
 Oh my god.

00:00:39.910 --> 00:00:42.670 line:84%
I flerken love this
movie, especially because

00:00:42.670 --> 00:00:43.750 line:90%
of all the '90s goodness.

00:00:43.750 --> 00:00:45.290 line:84%
I'm talking fashion,
soundtracks.

00:00:45.290 --> 00:00:46.090 line:90%
So good.

00:00:46.090 --> 00:00:46.890 line:90%
 Oh, the settings.

00:00:46.890 --> 00:00:47.790 line:90%
Come on, Blockbuster Video.

00:00:47.790 --> 00:00:48.590 line:90%
Gourmet choice.

00:00:48.590 --> 00:00:49.430 line:90%
 Oh, a delight.

00:00:49.430 --> 00:00:50.230 line:90%
Bringing me back.

00:00:50.230 --> 00:00:52.120 line:10%
And we're going to be talking
more about the '90s today.

00:00:52.120 --> 00:00:54.580 line:84%
But I think first, we
should talk about the fact

00:00:54.580 --> 00:00:56.770 line:84%
that I got to chat with visual
effects supervisor Christopher

00:00:56.770 --> 00:00:58.900 line:84%
Townsend all about
creating Goose the Cat's

00:00:58.900 --> 00:01:01.570 line:84%
cool secret skills,
the Kree-Skrull battle,

00:01:01.570 --> 00:01:03.220 line:90%
and Captain Marvel's big fall.

00:01:03.220 --> 00:01:06.040 line:84%
 But spoiler warnings ahead
if you have not seen this film.

00:01:06.040 --> 00:01:08.530 line:84%
But for those of you who
have, you are in for a treat.

00:01:08.530 --> 00:01:09.430 line:90%
This is super cool.

00:01:09.430 --> 00:01:10.230 line:90%
Let's watch.

00:01:10.230 --> 00:01:11.894 line:90%
 Oh.

00:01:11.894 --> 00:01:15.261 line:10%
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:24.430 line:10%
 I am here with visual
effects supervisor

00:01:24.430 --> 00:01:25.460 line:10%
Christopher Townsend.

00:01:25.460 --> 00:01:26.330 line:84%
Hello.
- Hi.

00:01:26.330 --> 00:01:27.130 line:90%
How are you doing?

00:01:27.130 --> 00:01:28.190 line:90%
 I'm very well.

00:01:28.190 --> 00:01:30.220 line:84%
So everyone has seen
the film by now.

00:01:30.220 --> 00:01:32.140 line:84%
If not, what have you
been doing with your life?

00:01:32.140 --> 00:01:33.820 line:90%
Get it together, people.

00:01:33.820 --> 00:01:35.440 line:84%
I want to talk about some
of the visual effects

00:01:35.440 --> 00:01:37.300 line:84%
that we can finally kind
of discuss, because it's

00:01:37.300 --> 00:01:39.370 line:90%
coming home for home release.

00:01:39.370 --> 00:01:41.830 line:84%
So first of all, I
know we were all very

00:01:41.830 --> 00:01:44.020 line:90%
excited to meet Goose the Cat.

00:01:44.020 --> 00:01:47.320 line:84%
There's a lot more to Goose the
Cat than maybe meets the eye,

00:01:47.320 --> 00:01:49.210 line:84%
like a pocket universe
full of tentacles

00:01:49.210 --> 00:01:50.010 line:90%
or something like that.

00:01:50.010 --> 00:01:52.390 line:84%
CHRISTOPHER TOWNSEND:
Something like that, yes.

00:01:52.390 --> 00:01:56.800 line:84%
 As you're starting to
create this alien creature,

00:01:56.800 --> 00:01:58.850 line:90%
where do you start?

00:01:58.850 --> 00:01:59.650 line:90%
 I think with--

00:01:59.650 --> 00:02:03.130 line:84%
as with most of these things,
with sort of these characters,

00:02:03.130 --> 00:02:04.840 line:90%
you go back to the comics.

00:02:04.840 --> 00:02:06.770 line:84%
And you look at the comics,
and you look at poster art,

00:02:06.770 --> 00:02:09.220 line:84%
and you look at the art
that's been done of,

00:02:09.220 --> 00:02:10.840 line:90%
what is the flerken?

00:02:10.840 --> 00:02:16.840 line:84%
So it's this big gooey, goopy,
terrifically sized monster sort

00:02:16.840 --> 00:02:18.550 line:84%
of thing that bursts
out of this cat,

00:02:18.550 --> 00:02:20.250 line:90%
and then goes back inside again.

00:02:20.250 --> 00:02:22.420 line:84%
And I think the
fun part was trying

00:02:22.420 --> 00:02:24.760 line:84%
to have that juxtaposition
between the two.

00:02:24.760 --> 00:02:27.020 line:84%
 And when you're bringing
that to life, obviously,

00:02:27.020 --> 00:02:31.270 line:84%
the flerken will
interact with the actors.

00:02:31.270 --> 00:02:33.880 line:84%
How do you get him to
interact with other characters

00:02:33.880 --> 00:02:35.200 line:90%
and pull it all together?

00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:37.330 line:84%
 It's all very carefully,
carefully orchestrated.

00:02:37.330 --> 00:02:40.390 line:84%
We have one particular scene
where the elite fighting force,

00:02:40.390 --> 00:02:44.500 line:84%
the Kree guards are coming in
and are being slammed around.

00:02:44.500 --> 00:02:49.570 line:84%
So we literally had stunts
go and rig up on our set

00:02:49.570 --> 00:02:52.060 line:84%
with wires, and actually
had these characters

00:02:52.060 --> 00:02:54.680 line:84%
being slammed around and moved,
and flipped, and flopped,

00:02:54.680 --> 00:02:55.480 line:90%
and things.

00:02:55.480 --> 00:02:57.760 line:10%
All that stuff is
very carefully planned

00:02:57.760 --> 00:03:01.100 line:10%
out in our pre-visualization
moment in our previous time.

00:03:01.100 --> 00:03:03.700 line:10%
And we figure out exactly how--

00:03:03.700 --> 00:03:05.830 line:10%
what the moves need
to be based on what

00:03:05.830 --> 00:03:07.510 line:10%
the tentacles are going to do.

00:03:07.510 --> 00:03:09.460 line:90%
So you sort of work backwards.

00:03:09.460 --> 00:03:11.440 line:84%
That's where visual effects
sort of fits in the middle,

00:03:11.440 --> 00:03:12.240 line:90%
as it were.

00:03:12.240 --> 00:03:14.650 line:84%
 So speaking of the
Kree and the Skrulls,

00:03:14.650 --> 00:03:18.440 line:84%
there is this large fight
between the two of them.

00:03:18.440 --> 00:03:22.090 line:84%
And there are a lot
of characters there.

00:03:22.090 --> 00:03:24.880 line:10%
How many characters
are being brought

00:03:24.880 --> 00:03:25.990 line:10%
in through visual effects?

00:03:25.990 --> 00:03:28.360 line:10%
And how many are actually there?

00:03:28.360 --> 00:03:29.760 line:10%
 We actually shot out--

00:03:29.760 --> 00:03:32.650 line:10%
there's a scene called
Torfa on the planet Torfa.

00:03:32.650 --> 00:03:35.980 line:84%
And we went out and we
shot this at a quarry

00:03:35.980 --> 00:03:37.630 line:90%
for a couple of weeks.

00:03:37.630 --> 00:03:40.120 line:84%
Because of the complexity
of you're shooting outside,

00:03:40.120 --> 00:03:43.720 line:84%
you're shooting at night, you're
shooting in fog, which is never

00:03:43.720 --> 00:03:45.250 line:84%
the same, all these
sort of things

00:03:45.250 --> 00:03:49.090 line:84%
made it incredibly difficult to
actually do it, to pull it off.

00:03:49.090 --> 00:03:50.920 line:10%
But I think what you see
at the end is this sort

00:03:50.920 --> 00:03:52.870 line:10%
of big wide scope of things.

00:03:52.870 --> 00:03:57.670 line:10%
There are maybe 40 or so
real actors in full makeup

00:03:57.670 --> 00:04:00.640 line:10%
and prosthetic masks,
and helmets, and costume,

00:04:00.640 --> 00:04:01.870 line:10%
and everything
else running around

00:04:01.870 --> 00:04:05.200 line:10%
in that sandy sort of quarry.

00:04:05.200 --> 00:04:09.190 line:84%
And then we've added easily
just as many characters

00:04:09.190 --> 00:04:11.320 line:90%
on top in digitally.

00:04:11.320 --> 00:04:13.000 line:84%
It's really a mix
between the sort

00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:17.170 line:84%
of the traditional sort of
stunt work and visual effects.

00:04:17.170 --> 00:04:19.390 line:10%
 There is an epic
scene at the end where

00:04:19.390 --> 00:04:21.700 line:10%
Captain Marvel is falling.

00:04:21.700 --> 00:04:23.530 line:10%
It is harrowing.

00:04:23.530 --> 00:04:25.360 line:10%
How do you place that?

00:04:25.360 --> 00:04:28.110 line:10%
Because obviously, we
can't drop Brie Larson.

00:04:28.110 --> 00:04:30.730 line:84%
 Yeah, so a lot of-- obviously,
a lot of what we do is

00:04:30.730 --> 00:04:33.920 line:84%
you're trying to make
the impossible possible,

00:04:33.920 --> 00:04:35.320 line:84%
and also making
it, hopefully, look

00:04:35.320 --> 00:04:38.540 line:84%
real so that an audience is
there and never questions it.

00:04:38.540 --> 00:04:40.240 line:84%
And there are many things
we could have tried.

00:04:40.240 --> 00:04:41.950 line:90%
We could have tried skydiving.

00:04:41.950 --> 00:04:43.810 line:84%
We could have tried these
sort of wind tunnels.

00:04:43.810 --> 00:04:45.340 line:84%
We could have
tried her on wires.

00:04:45.340 --> 00:04:47.510 line:84%
We could've tried all
sorts of different things.

00:04:47.510 --> 00:04:50.860 line:84%
One of the things we
realized very quickly

00:04:50.860 --> 00:04:53.650 line:84%
was that for what we needed
for her in this very specific

00:04:53.650 --> 00:04:58.000 line:84%
moment is to be able just to
use a digital double of her,

00:04:58.000 --> 00:05:00.070 line:84%
and be able to just
close in on her face

00:05:00.070 --> 00:05:01.810 line:84%
and be able to use her
face and her expressions

00:05:01.810 --> 00:05:02.890 line:90%
where necessary.

00:05:02.890 --> 00:05:04.540 line:84%
 And there's some other
performance involved,

00:05:04.540 --> 00:05:07.160 line:84%
too, because there are some
folks in green screen suits

00:05:07.160 --> 00:05:07.960 line:90%
as well.

00:05:07.960 --> 00:05:08.760 line:90%
 There are.

00:05:08.760 --> 00:05:10.750 line:84%
There are people there
that are moving her around

00:05:10.750 --> 00:05:11.620 line:90%
in the blue screen suits.

00:05:11.620 --> 00:05:14.410 line:84%
And they're using that to
try and puppeteer her to make

00:05:14.410 --> 00:05:16.000 line:90%
it feel like she's floating.

00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:17.590 line:84%
Because one of the
problems is-- obviously,

00:05:17.590 --> 00:05:19.600 line:84%
when you're literally
on wires, you're

00:05:19.600 --> 00:05:21.670 line:84%
being supported in a
cradle, or if you're

00:05:21.670 --> 00:05:24.690 line:84%
on a backboard where you're
just being supported,

00:05:24.690 --> 00:05:26.440 line:90%
your legs tend to go down.

00:05:26.440 --> 00:05:28.420 line:84%
So you need to make
it feel like someone

00:05:28.420 --> 00:05:31.270 line:84%
is moving around in a more
naturalistic way as you would

00:05:31.270 --> 00:05:32.230 line:90%
when falling.

00:05:32.230 --> 00:05:34.270 line:84%
We used a lot of
that, not only--

00:05:34.270 --> 00:05:36.340 line:84%
some of it is actually
literally in the film.

00:05:36.340 --> 00:05:38.110 line:84%
Also, a lot of it was
just used as reference

00:05:38.110 --> 00:05:41.890 line:84%
so that we can see how Brie's
body moves in a particular way

00:05:41.890 --> 00:05:44.350 line:84%
and how the costume
moves in a particular way

00:05:44.350 --> 00:05:46.780 line:84%
when she's doing a particular
thing with her arms or legs.

00:05:46.780 --> 00:05:49.320 line:84%
We also shot elements
just of her face.

00:05:49.320 --> 00:05:52.690 line:84%
And so you can imagine we
were sitting in a studio

00:05:52.690 --> 00:05:55.770 line:84%
with her sitting in a chair,
and she's got the helmet on.

00:05:55.770 --> 00:05:57.700 line:90%
And we'd say, OK, look scared!

00:05:57.700 --> 00:05:58.600 line:90%
OK, look over to your left!

00:05:58.600 --> 00:05:59.620 line:90%
Look over to your right!

00:05:59.620 --> 00:06:00.910 line:90%
Oh, now this is happening!

00:06:00.910 --> 00:06:04.000 line:84%
And she was a real
trooper and amazing

00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:06.520 line:84%
to watch, a true
professional as an actor

00:06:06.520 --> 00:06:08.680 line:84%
being able to react
to that, and pretend

00:06:08.680 --> 00:06:10.767 line:84%
that they're falling and
panicking, and looking.

00:06:10.767 --> 00:06:12.100 line:84%
LORRAINE CINK: But
it's just right here.

00:06:12.100 --> 00:06:13.467 line:84%
CHRISTOPHER TOWNSEND:
And it's just here.

00:06:13.467 --> 00:06:16.480 line:10%
And all we're capturing is
just her face and expressions.

00:06:16.480 --> 00:06:18.220 line:10%
And we take all of
that information

00:06:18.220 --> 00:06:20.320 line:10%
and then we would map that.

00:06:20.320 --> 00:06:23.660 line:10%
We would project that
onto a CG version of her.

00:06:23.660 --> 00:06:26.240 line:10%
So what you see in the
final film is generally

00:06:26.240 --> 00:06:29.060 line:10%
a digital version
of her falling,

00:06:29.060 --> 00:06:31.970 line:10%
but with her performance
mapped on her face,

00:06:31.970 --> 00:06:35.720 line:10%
put onto the digital
version of her.

00:06:35.720 --> 00:06:39.620 line:84%
 So you also got
to create a very

00:06:39.620 --> 00:06:41.300 line:84%
interesting realm
that we've never

00:06:41.300 --> 00:06:42.980 line:90%
seen in the Marvel universe.

00:06:42.980 --> 00:06:44.570 line:90%
And it's hard to say.

00:06:44.570 --> 00:06:46.160 line:84%
It's more of a
consciousness, we'll

00:06:46.160 --> 00:06:48.920 line:90%
say, the Supreme Intelligence.

00:06:48.920 --> 00:06:55.190 line:84%
How did you build that
interaction world brain space?

00:06:55.190 --> 00:06:56.330 line:90%
What do you call it?

00:06:56.330 --> 00:06:59.030 line:84%
 We call it the Supreme
Intelligent Chamber--

00:06:59.030 --> 00:07:00.050 line:90%
Intelligence Chamber.

00:07:00.050 --> 00:07:03.413 line:84%
And I think it was a fascinating
sort of bit of storytelling

00:07:03.413 --> 00:07:04.580 line:84%
that we were trying
to do in there.

00:07:04.580 --> 00:07:06.590 line:84%
There's a lot of exposition
that happens in that room.

00:07:06.590 --> 00:07:10.040 line:84%
There's a lot of sort of
definition of the characters

00:07:10.040 --> 00:07:11.510 line:90%
that happen.

00:07:11.510 --> 00:07:17.490 line:84%
But the idea was that the
room exists in a reality.

00:07:17.490 --> 00:07:19.190 line:84%
It's a virtual reality,
but it should never

00:07:19.190 --> 00:07:20.700 line:90%
look like virtual reality.

00:07:20.700 --> 00:07:22.820 line:84%
It should always feel
like a very real space.

00:07:22.820 --> 00:07:24.620 line:84%
But we wanted to keep
it a little bit surreal.

00:07:24.620 --> 00:07:26.300 line:84%
And we went through
many iterations

00:07:26.300 --> 00:07:32.480 line:84%
from massive green hexagonal
blocks to liquid worlds

00:07:32.480 --> 00:07:37.370 line:84%
to almost Salvador
Dali sort of art.

00:07:37.370 --> 00:07:38.990 line:84%
We went through all
sorts of things,

00:07:38.990 --> 00:07:40.880 line:84%
but eventually ended
up back at this very

00:07:40.880 --> 00:07:44.630 line:84%
minimalist, sort of almost a
white room and a clean room.

00:07:44.630 --> 00:07:46.820 line:84%
And the idea being
that you can almost--

00:07:46.820 --> 00:07:50.230 line:84%
whatever you want to conjure in
that room, you can make happen.

00:07:50.230 --> 00:07:51.830 line:84%
There's obviously-- there's
a point in the movie

00:07:51.830 --> 00:07:54.110 line:84%
where we twist, and
things get a bit

00:07:54.110 --> 00:07:56.330 line:90%
more violent and aggressive.

00:07:56.330 --> 00:07:58.550 line:84%
And then the room itself
begins to collapse.

00:07:58.550 --> 00:08:00.530 line:84%
And it was a really
interesting challenge

00:08:00.530 --> 00:08:02.510 line:84%
to try and figure out how
to create something which

00:08:02.510 --> 00:08:05.870 line:84%
would sort of satisfy both
the serene and the violent

00:08:05.870 --> 00:08:07.250 line:90%
all at once.

00:08:07.250 --> 00:08:10.040 line:84%
 Well, it is beautiful
and very serene.

00:08:10.040 --> 00:08:12.500 line:84%
And I would very much like
to have that in my home.

00:08:12.500 --> 00:08:14.070 line:90%
Not the latter half--

00:08:14.070 --> 00:08:14.870 line:90%
 Yes.

00:08:14.870 --> 00:08:16.730 line:90%
 But the first part, very nice.

00:08:16.730 --> 00:08:17.900 line:90%
 Yes.

00:08:17.900 --> 00:08:19.110 line:90%
 Thank you so much.

00:08:19.110 --> 00:08:19.980 line:90%
 You're very welcome.

00:08:19.980 --> 00:08:21.380 line:90%
 Oh, my pleasure.

00:08:21.380 --> 00:08:23.780 line:84%
You guys, be sure to watch
Marvel Studios' Captain Marvel.

00:08:23.780 --> 00:08:26.020 line:84%
It's available for
digital download now.

00:08:30.020 --> 00:08:31.200 line:90%
 So many visual effects.

00:08:31.200 --> 00:08:33.990 line:84%
The brains behind these
things are bigger than me.

00:08:33.990 --> 00:08:34.870 line:90%
 It's mind-blowing.

00:08:34.870 --> 00:08:36.900 line:90%
It really is mind-blowing.

00:08:36.900 --> 00:08:39.000 line:84%
But you know what
else is mind-blowing?

00:08:39.000 --> 00:08:43.232 line:84%
I've got one bit of itty bitty
kitty trivia for you guys.

00:08:43.232 --> 00:08:45.120 line:84%
 I was waiting for
the rest of that.

00:08:45.120 --> 00:08:46.230 line:90%
 I think this is so cool.

00:08:46.230 --> 00:08:48.840 line:84%
You know, ginger cats,
IRL, In Real Life,

00:08:48.840 --> 00:08:50.160 line:90%
tend to be genetically male.

00:08:50.160 --> 00:08:53.220 line:84%
So our first hint that Goose
is a little bit different

00:08:53.220 --> 00:08:55.310 line:90%
is that she is female.

00:08:55.310 --> 00:08:56.535 line:84%
 All the clues.
All the clues.

00:08:56.535 --> 00:08:57.300 line:84%
 Yeah.
Isn't that good?

00:08:57.300 --> 00:08:57.990 line:84%
 You fine out
all the knowledge.

00:08:57.990 --> 00:08:58.840 line:84%
I like that.
Yeah.

00:08:58.840 --> 00:08:59.300 line:90%
 Yeah.

00:08:59.300 --> 00:09:00.767 line:84%
 Listen, there are so
many more fun details

00:09:00.767 --> 00:09:02.070 line:84%
from the comic books
about flerkens.

00:09:02.070 --> 00:09:03.510 line:84%
- Sure.
- Let's talk about those, right?

